WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.211
A concept for what a ride app could do
after a one star rating.

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:10.074
After a bad ride, riders often stay quiet.
One star just gets a thank you, and

3
00:00:10.074 --> 00:00:12.337
the same driver can show up again.

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.253
So the response matches the rating. The
worse the ride, the more the app

5
00:00:17.253 --> 00:00:17.564
offers.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.534
One star gets one question: avoid this
driver in the future? The rider

7
00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.627
decides, and it can be undone.

8
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.574
A middling ride gets optional reasons. A
good ride gets a quick thanks, then

9
00:00:29.574 --> 00:00:30.824
back to the map.

10
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.991
So quiet riders still get heard, without
having to speak up.
